{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal","id":961192,"title":"Problem \u2013 Nameless mage in Pentacle cabal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-31T13:14:16-07:00","id":961192,"title":"Problem \u2013 Nameless mage in Pentacle cabal","content":"Lately, I have a greatest <b>Mage </b>ST headache \u2013 Nameless PC with Pentacle cabal of others PC. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's constant pain. Example:<br /> Storyteller: What do you do?<br /> Rest of cabal: We go do things for mentors/Consilium/Orders.<br /> Nameless: I go to library to read about occult and learn about magic on my own terms.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s like all possible answers are \u2018I\u2019m brooding in corner until someone need me to call ghosts/spirits\u2019. PC has rejected offers of mentoring from Silver Ladder, Seers of Throne, Guardians of Veil and even Free Council representatives. ( In this sequence, Adamantine Arrow also do not sounds as fitting for her. )<br /> <br /> As 2E setting, Nameless are <i>not</i> having access to Pentacles Orders supplies and help - <b>I\u2019m wondering on to how to show the PC that what she is doing is stupid to not join any Order, from in-game perspective.</b><br /> <br /> <b>And how Nameless in general are convinced to join Orders at large?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T13:49:53-07:00","id":961219,"title":"","content":"Why do you call someone playing their concept straight &quot;stupid&quot;? A lot of people like being self reliant and dislikes having to rely on outside sources. Just give her opportunities for self study. If one of her Path Arcana is at least level 3, she can use them as a source of material. Instead of strong arming her into an Order, throw her a mysterious book to research, occult artifact that talks to her in her dreams, or some other mystery to explore that will occupy usual &quot;order space&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:20:39-07:00","id":961232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal#post961192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lately, I have a greatest <b>Mage </b>ST headache \u2013 Nameless PC with Pentacle cabal of others PC. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It's constant pain. Example:<br /> Storyteller: What do you do?<br /> Rest of cabal: We go do things for mentors/Consilium/Orders.<br /> Nameless: I go to library to read about occult and learn about magic on my own terms.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s like all possible answers are \u2018I\u2019m brooding in corner until someone need me to call ghosts/spirits\u2019. PC has rejected offers of mentoring from Silver Ladder, Seers of Throne, Guardians of Veil and even Free Council representatives. ( In this sequence, Adamantine Arrow also do not sounds as fitting for her. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay from what you saying the problem seems more that your game is geared towards &quot;Figure of power gives you X quest&quot; and this players just doesnt want to engage in that. I have played a caitiff vampire in masquerade who had his own agendas that had little to do with what the prince/clan leader wanted or give it to other players.<br /> <br /> Even in mage ascension i played a Order of hermes mage whose attitude to the whole ascension war/order was &quot;meh, i only care about living in peace in my little occult shop i dont care about no concensual reality&quot; and the play was the inter personal conflict with his life and his cabal. He tagged along with the cabal because they were his &quot;friends&quot; (in the looses term of the word) and he would tag along because something interesting might happen or he would learn something new.<br /> <br /> So my advice is to talk in private to this player and ask him if maybe the kind of game you are running is not for his taste (hence his gangrel attitude) or try to work up why he would tag along. Maybe he doesnt gain anything but hey, if they doing magic stuff it could be fun/learn something new.<br /> <br /> If she doesnt wanna engage in consilium politics but also doesnt have an personal stake in nothing else them she is really could just be replace with a fetish that cast &quot;talk to ghost&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal#post961192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As 2E setting, Nameless are <i>not</i> having access to Pentacles Orders supplies and help - <b>I\u2019m wondering on to how to show the PC that what she is doing is stupid to not join any Order, from in-game perspective.</b><br /> <br /> <b>And how Nameless in general are convinced to join Orders at large?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Problem with this is that while the setting sells you that the life of the nameless is harsh the mechanics dont support that. You can raise your main arcanum up to 5 and then learn the rest by your cabal or none at all. From what you said this PC started with the library merit so actually she joining a order is stupid in this case.<br /> <br /> What she gains from joining an order? supplies she already has or dont care for? Allies she already has in her cabal or new one she doesnt care for? Does she has any agency or objectives that needs an order for? Because it sounds this particular mage doesnt gain anything from joining an order.<br /> <br /> Now that said if you wanna force the issue with in-game consequences, which in my opinion is a bad idea and i recommend to talk to the player first because nobody likes to get the rug pulled from under their feet, but if you still feel you need to &quot;show&quot; this player the consecuences of no choosing one the orders you can use....<br /> <br /> A crime magical crime is commited, the cabal is the main suspect but their respective orders vouch for the members leaving the nameless as the most likely scapegoat. He gets sentenced with something not life ending/pc terminating so he sees the consecuences of not choosing his side.<br /> <br /> Burn her library and thus force her to join an order to get the help of one order.<br /> <br /> Make a situation in which something the PC cares about is in danger but the orders forbid the rest of the cabals to interfere because is too dangerous to risk members of the order leaving him alone to sink in how having no allies doesnt work.<br /> <br /> I will however stress out that while this ideas work on paper using them will most likely (though not always) cause the player to resent you, the DM, and thus the order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":".  Misspelled order with cabal :P 08-31-2016, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:22:34-07:00","id":961234,"title":"","content":"Or don't bother to fill the Order space at all. Just leave it empty, if that's the way the player wants to play then let them. They can still fully engage in the Mysteries that the rest of the cabal are pursuing, they'll just be limited in the resources they can throw at it because they can't call on an Order. If it they're cool with it then cool. You have a unique opportunity to play up the difference of being in or out of an Order, and it's what you make it.<br /> <br /> The easiest way to make the difference of being in or out of an Order apparent is probably just for the Orders to make it clear to their members in the cabal that sharing Order secrets (Rote skills, rotes, imbued items, etc) with their uninitiated friend is frowned upon and then just leave it alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:23:52-07:00","id":961236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do you call someone playing their concept straight &quot;stupid&quot;? </div> </div> </div>I don't get the impression they've got a concept. It sounds more like they don't know what they're doing and being kinda difficult as a result. It's not uncommon behaviour for players who are kinda checked out of the game. Personally I'd recommend talking to the player about this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961219#post961219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A lot of people like being self reliant and dislikes having to rely on outside sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they'll use a public library.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:25:29-07:00","id":961238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961234#post961234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or don't bother to fill the Order space at all. Just leave it empty, if that's the way the player wants to play then let them. They can still fully engage in the Mysteries that the rest of the cabal are pursuing, they'll just be limited in the resources they can throw at it because they can't call on an Order. If it they're cool with it then cool. You have a unique opportunity to play up the difference of being in or out of an Order, and it's what you make it.<br /> <br /> The easiest way to make the difference of being in or out of an Order apparent is probably just for the Orders to make it clear to their members in the cabal that sharing Order secrets (Rote skills, rotes, imbued items, etc) with their uninitiated friend is frowned upon and then just leave it alone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the problem is less than this player i asking for this concept and more that Wyrdhamster already said yes, and this player is just constantly playing the gangrel card (&quot;im just gonna brood in the corner until combat start) and refuses to engage in plots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:34:26-07:00","id":961243,"title":"","content":"And I'm saying that's fine and he doesn't need to make any special effort to engage the player. Just put the boundaries down between what's in and out of the Order and stick to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T16:14:54-07:00","id":961276,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but public library doesn't require active membership in a dangerous religious cult. Which is, basically, what Orders are. The difference here is &quot;are you going to enter this creepy occult organization, do their creepy rituals, and participate in their weird and potentially dangerous faith&quot;? I know that joining an Order seems like a no brainer for players, but I can see thousands and hundreds of reasons why a character wouldn't want to do that.<br /> <br /> What are character's aspirations? What is her Obsession? If the character is capable of ghost/spirit calling, then you probably can make exciting plots about exploring magic on your own by exploring ghost and spirit mysteries; if only option you present to them is brooding in library, then they will brood in library. If they have their Path Arcanum at 3, they can Summon things to ask questions and learn from.<br /> I mean, it's a game about exploring Mysteries, not playing Consilium Politics. They don't want to engage with political plots? Don't force them to. I can sympathize, because I find political plots incredibly boring myself, and also like playing self-taught characters that explore and learn on their own. Some people just find that more fun, and not having access to Order's resources might be a boon for them, because hey, what's so fun about relying on others?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Problem with this is that while the setting sells you that the life of the nameless is harsh the mechanics dont support that. You can raise your main arcanum up to 5 and then learn the rest by your cabal or none at all. From what you said this PC started with the library merit so actually she joining a order is stupid in this case. </div> </div> </div>Nameless Mage doesn't get 6 Rotes, they don't get 3 Rote Specialties, and they don't get 2 dots of merits. Being Nameless is extremely harsh - you lose out about 11 XP.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Why not enlist them as a order-less member of the Consilium? They are already in a Cabal, so Consilium has means to control them and make sure they follow their laws anyway - rest of the team basically is responsible for them and guarantees that they are a good member of the society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-31-2016, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T16:51:25-07:00","id":961286,"title":"","content":"I think the best piece o advice so far has been the &quot;talk to the player&quot;. See what the problem is exactly, and figure it out between the two of you. Once that's out of the way, however, I'd say that not belonging to an Order doesn't mean that the character can't have any dealings with an Order. In fact, it opens new and interesting avenues. They could be used as a Freelancer or Mercenary (as WHW said, there's a handful of things any Order could offer the character as payment). Or, they could be simply be in good terms with some other Mages. Maybe a member of the Mysterium happens to notice the book they're reading and engages them in a conversation. Or a Thyrsus' familiar takes a liking to them. Or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T18:08:44-07:00","id":961315,"title":"","content":"^I feel a Shadowrunner Mage coming on.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> I'm not advocating freezing the PC out of things that interest them just because they don't want to be in an Order. I'm just saying that there's a fairly clear line between being in or out of an Order and if it's kept clear then really it's all good. I could see a interesting storyline with the theme of disparity of power between the Solitaires and the Orders. The question and temptation being the Orders give so much, but is it worth it, and what might a Solitaire have to do to try and make up for the lack? There's also the temptation to the other PCs who are in Orders, maybe they want to share their secrets with their Solitaire friend, but it's a big no-no in social and political terms. <br /> <br /> I actually have a sort of similar situation going on in another game. One of my PCs is a Guardian, but sort of bad at it. One of them is being courted for membership in an Order having just Awakened not long ago. The third got inducted into the Choir of Hashmallim almost immediately after Awakening and has rejected membership in the Orders because he considers his first allegiance to be to God and fighting the forces of darkness and doesn't want to run the risk of a conflict of interest by buying into an Order's ideology. Second PC is sweet on the first PC. My hope is to kind of nudge the second into an Order and then spill the beans to the third, or have the first falter a little and give away secrets to either and then spin off some more stories from there. Player #3 is far and away the most competent Mage player in my group so not being as equipped as #1 (And potentially #2) doesn't bother him much. I guess my point is, just because you have one PC not in an Order, it's not a problem as long as you can capitalize on it instead of whinging.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> Btw, have the Mysterium approached this character? I mean, even if it's rejected there's some potential there. The Mysterium are pretty much the most social Order, but they're also very fond of tucking themselves away in libraries of arcane lore and ignoring the outside world. Basically, the character doesn't have to join, it's just one more possible plot thing that can be developed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T18:22:04-07:00","id":961322,"title":"","content":"I know you are not advocating it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I actually agree with your other post about using this opportunity to highlight the difference between an Order-less Mage and a Order member. <br /> ...aren't Solitaries mages without cabals, not uninitiated Mages?<br /> My problem with &quot;secrets sharing&quot; is that, well...there aren't really any secrets worth giving away. Like, almost everything that's &quot;Secret Order Stuff&quot; is actually unusable without being an Order Member - you can't get Order Merits (because you lack dot of Status to buy them), they can't use your Order Tools and Rote Skills anyway...pretty much only things that you could consider a Secret Order Stuff that can be given to someone is Rotes and stuff you borrow using Order Status. <br /> Anyway, I guess listing some alternate ways for engaging the player might be helpful here; Wyrd tends to rely heavily on NPCs, so player refusing to engage with an Order might be somewhat new situation to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T18:56:51-07:00","id":961335,"title":"","content":"I think you're right about Solitaires, I just used it as convenient shorthand.<br /> <br /> I guess when I'm running a game the &quot;Secret Order Stuff&quot; is something I'd allow a PC (Or a particular sort of NPC) to teach to a non-member. Order Tools and Rote Skills aren't even merits and are possibly the most likely kind of secret to be leaked, stuff borrowed from an Order might get &quot;accidentally&quot; shared with a non-member, that kind of thing. I tend to be open to tweaking things too, so I'd consider letting characters take Merits without meeting all the prerequisites for an interesting enough reason.<br /> <br /> Although, now I have this idea of doing a stealth initiation where the prospect has secrets &quot;leaked&quot; to them but is actually being subtly inducted. By the end the prospect could be a full blown member of an Order and not even know it, with the right handling. Then for the reveal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T20:01:08-07:00","id":961368,"title":"","content":"It may be that all you require is a small change in set dressing or how you present things. Instead of setting your players off on a task by having a mentor assign it to them, you throw a bone directly into their path and let them pick it up on their own initiative. For example: instead of having the Mysterium assign the cabal to find the lost tomb of Martek, the characters find a possible map to the lost tomb and rush off with visions of treasure as their motivation. Instead of having the Arrow assign them to investigate a series of mysterious disappearances among the sleepers someone connected to them disappears, or maybe the heroes stumble upon an abduction in progress. Most players will pursue an interesting story on their own, that is why they are playing the game, you just need a hook that doesn't require membership in the army or police force. Also, just because a character isn't a member of an order doesn't mean they can't have a place in Mage society. You can go to a community dinner without having to drink the punch.<br /> \u200bI would also point out that if your player wants to play the outsider, that they are not just being difficult to ruin it for everyone else, then as ST you should try to find a way to let them play the character they want, especially if you can exploit it for everyone's enjoyment. The other players may enjoy 'protecting' their friend from the orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 08-31-2016, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T01:02:34-07:00","id":961512,"title":"","content":"Big question that spring to my mind reading answers - <b>Is Mysterium sharing Atheneum lore with Nameless?</b> Order is based on the idea of reputation and favors, on what front Nameless does not sound as reliable and at least from my reading of <b>Mysterium</b> book, it sounds they would closed the doors before one without any Pentacle affiliation. Even Free Council has higher esteem in their eyes.<br /> <br /> Some thoughts and answers from previous posts:<br /> 1. I talked about it with player before. Her answer on topic was 'PC do not like any of Orders and want to pursue magic on my own. MAYBE if some ghost mage would point me to Mysterium, I may rethink my stance.' There is also thing that come out in last game session - Mysterium has Protocol to not Lie to others and PC is not agreeing with that stance. She has strong anti-Sleeper streak like 'Humans are stupid, many do not deserve magic', so maybe playing on darker parts of Mysterium would work - <i>if</i> they would not be so trustworthy in first place.<br /> <br /> 2. Nameless PC is studying occult in Harvard University Library in Boston, reading Sleepers books. I will maybe let her take one dot higher in Occult Skill if she will be pursuing it still, but I'm not sure is it should be 'free', as rest part of cabal in Pentacle is getting it. Pentacle is giving you for free 'reality works this and that, occult is all about this'. Nameless do not get that, from my reading of setting. She still get High Speech before from few days with Free Council and her preAwakening research on subject.<br /> <br /> 3. Unofficially, I know from other players her attitude is irking them too. I hope that issue will resolve quickly, as it can lead to some players issues in longer play.<br /> <br /> 4. I wonder how much Rotes, Rotes Specialties and Order Merits can be incentive to players? As we play whole initiation into Orders thing ( jumping for a few days at once, but still playing it out ) I wonder when you will see real difference in training.<br /> <br /> 5. How much things from point 4 are 'hush-hush' thing in contacts with Nameless? If Pentacle PC share a Rote with Nameless, what can it lead from her superiors in Order? Is it more \u2018One more action like this, and you will become Nameless like her!\u2019 or like \u2018We understand you spend time together, but please do not share them with it \u2013 it makes look you bad and can hinder you rise in Order \u2018. Is Nameless ban to take Atheneum lore? I suspect that Free Council Lorehouse will still be open to her, but I think it will be <i>very </i>poor substitute in Boston, run by the Dead Wrens \u2018pirates\u2019.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T02:03:35-07:00","id":961528,"title":"","content":"2) Raising your Occult in a mundane library is fine. Regular people do it all the time. It probably shouldn't be free though.<br /> <br /> 4) Those are going to be smaller incentives than the social ones that Orders provide.<br /> <br /> 5) The reaction of the Orders is strictly up to you and can be any of those you described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T07:35:07-07:00","id":961655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961276#post961276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nameless Mage doesn't get 6 Rotes, they don't get 3 Rote Specialties, and they don't get 2 dots of merits. Being Nameless is extremely harsh - you lose out about 11 XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have clarified, the mechanic doesnt restrict the character development after chargen. Though im looking for it and cant find where it says that nameless mages cant start with rotes.<br /> <br /> But that aside, those 11 points of xp &quot;lost&quot; are assuming that one uses chargen rules as written meaning &quot;well stablish mages&quot; but if you run newly awakened not so much but thats beside the point that its not particularly harsh. 11 point automatically spent in think you PC dont care for is not &quot;harsh&quot; (and bear in mind that the mystery cult merit bypass that). +1 in dices is &quot;nice&quot; but not game breaking and considering starting mage have very little yantras they could apply high speech can be replace with anything else. So its basically 2 point for 1 point in occult you miss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961512#post961512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I talked about it with player before. Her answer on topic was 'PC do not like any of Orders and want to pursue magic on my own. MAYBE if some ghost mage would point me to Mysterium, I may rethink my stance.' There is also thing that come out in last game session - Mysterium has Protocol to not Lie to others and PC is not agreeing with that stance. She has strong anti-Sleeper streak like 'Humans are stupid, many do not deserve magic', so maybe playing on darker parts of Mysterium would work - <i>if</i> they would not be so trustworthy in first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might have it wrong here. The mysterium protocol is to not lie to other mages about magic knowledge directly. They can lie as much as they want to sleepers, and they can lie to other mages but when a mage ask them &quot;does X magic thingie exist&quot; and its classified and/or dont feel like answering they can say &quot;i cant confirm or deny that&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961512#post961512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Nameless PC is studying occult in Harvard University Library in Boston, reading Sleepers books. I will maybe let her take one dot higher in Occult Skill if she will be pursuing it still, but I'm not sure is it should be 'free', as rest part of cabal in Pentacle is getting it. Pentacle is giving you for free 'reality works this and that, occult is all about this'. Nameless do not get that, from my reading of setting. She still get High Speech before from few days with Free Council and her preAwakening research on subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless she take mystery cult initiation, it shouldnt be free.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961512#post961512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Unofficially, I know from other players her attitude is irking them too. I hope that issue will resolve quickly, as it can lead to some players issues in longer play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, its sounds less the problem is that she is nameless and more than the character has very little agency and doesnt play along.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961512#post961512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. I wonder how much Rotes, Rotes Specialties and Order Merits can be incentive to players? As we play whole initiation into Orders thing ( jumping for a few days at once, but still playing it out ) I wonder when you will see real difference in training.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very very little. Like i said above each of those can be bypasses/arent a big deal mechanically. And this player, read the chargen rules, read what she would be missing mechanically by choosing nameless and went along with it. You are barking at the wrong tree there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-01-2016, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T08:56:15-07:00","id":961688,"title":"","content":"Let\u2019s look at the benefits of joining an order.<br /> <br /> The High Speech merit at one dot for free. Yeah that\u2019s a big help.<br /> <br /> One dot in the Occult Skill for free. Two experience points worth of benefit, also helpful.<br /> <br /> One dot in Order status which grants access to the Order\u2019s special merits. What makes Order status special is that it is basically a modular advantage. Anything you need that the order can provide can be gained with Order status. If you join the Seers of the Throne that dot of Order status also counts as a dot of resources.<br /> <br /> Even Nameless mages get three rotes.<br /> <br /> Four experience points of stuff for free. Thus ends the benefits.<br /> <br /> Drawbacks of joining an Order.<br /> <br /> You now have the Connected condition with regard to that order (mage p 315), or at least that\u2019s how I read it. Basically whatever your order asks you to do you need to try to do it, as inconvenient as that might be. If you\u2019re a Seer you also have to contend with backstabbing peers and getting orders from pitiless inhuman masters. In other words Plot Hooks.<br /> <br /> I can see the appeal of being a nameless mage, honestly. You get to really choose your friends for yourself and focus on your own life. Your cabal can help you when you need friends and even without joining an order a nameless mage can still get status in the Concillium. Just think about it. She has no order so she is ideal for helping other mages settle disputes. Have mages across the Concillium start coming to her as a neutral arbiter. Have the Concillium teach her a rote for Display of Power (Prime 3) and offer training in Empathy and Persuasion. She could easily have Concillium status with no other duties than to preside over duels. What if people want to cheat? Does she accept bribes? What if someone wants to duel a Cabal mate? If she doesn\u2019t play favorites she can have most of the benefits of order status with few of the drawbacks.<br /> <br /> As far as plot hooks go all you have to do is involve the rest of the Cabal to get the Nameless in on the action. Just make it so the Cabal can\u2019t do the assignment without her.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T09:07:26-07:00","id":961697,"title":"","content":"If she has refused to join an Order where are you coming up with three Rotes for her to have learned? That's at least contingent on someone in an Order offering to reach her or a grimoire and guess who has most of those.<br /> <br /> Also, the neutral arbiter idea is possible, but unlikely. Inside the Pentacle the Mysterium is usually trusted as a go between because they have the most rigorous identification and ID checking system. Nameless are unknown quantities, and one way you can look at Mages is generally they aren't comfortable with those, which is why they obsess over knowing everything inside and out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T09:34:11-07:00","id":961718,"title":"","content":"I have a question concerning topic - <b>If PC is trained by the lone mentor from Order - but is <i>not</i> part of official local Caucus - is she treated as having full Order benefit?</b> Like I plan to put Mysterium Moros ghost mage as her possible mentor - Would she have benefits of Order from training under him?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961688#post961688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The High Speech merit at one dot for free. Yeah that\u2019s a big help.</div> </div> </div> </div>She has it from few days with Free Council cabal and her preAwakening studies over High Speech.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961688#post961688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Nameless mages get three rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Where</i> did you found that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Because 'free Rotes' where always in 1E incentive to join Orders in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961688#post961688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the appeal of being a nameless mage, honestly. You get to really choose your friends for yourself and focus on your own life. Your cabal can help you when you need friends and even without joining an order a nameless mage can still get status in the Concillium. Just think about it. She has no order so she is ideal for helping other mages settle disputes. Have mages across the Concillium start coming to her as a neutral arbiter. Have the Concillium teach her a rote for Display of Power (Prime 3) and offer training in Empathy and Persuasion. She could easily have Concillium status with no other duties than to preside over duels. What if people want to cheat? Does she accept bribes? What if someone wants to duel a Cabal mate? If she doesn\u2019t play favorites she can have most of the benefits of order status with few of the drawbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not see it in this example. PC is hates dearly one of Conciliors ( Khumeia from Boston ), so she cannot work with Consilium. Also, Orders just not freely teach Rotes to anyone around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-01-2016, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T10:07:46-07:00","id":961743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961697#post961697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If she has refused to join an Order where are you coming up with three Rotes for her to have learned? That's at least contingent on someone in an Order offering to reach her or a grimoire and guess who has most of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well this is a issue of mechanics over fluff, the rules indicates what a nameless doesnt start with and it doesnt mention that the PC doesnt starts with rotes. Fluff wise it depends on the individual PC, in this case if the nameless hanged out so much with the free council as to get High speech for free then it is enough justification to start with 3 rotes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961697#post961697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the neutral arbiter idea is possible, but unlikely. Inside the Pentacle the Mysterium is usually trusted as a go between because they have the most rigorous identification and ID checking system. Nameless are unknown quantities, and one way you can look at Mages is generally they aren't comfortable with those, which is why they obsess over knowing everything inside and out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the whole neutral arbitrer would be more the Lictor purview as they are traveling judges that offer neutral mediation by the lex magica. I could see the silver ladder taking umbrage with the pc meddling with that or the other orders liking having a non-SL mediator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961718#post961718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question concerning topic - <b>If PC is trained by the lone mentor from Order - but is <i>not</i> part of official local Caucus - is she treated as having full Order benefit?</b> Like I plan to put Mysterium Moros ghost mage as her possible mentor - Would she have benefits of Order from training under him?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say no, she would have to pass the initiation for that and that normally requires more than one mage. But is mostly blah blah symbolism BS explanation so it could go either way in your game. But more to the point, if the ghost mage is willing to entrust her to become part of the order then why the order doesnt want her? Because you can be a part of an order but not the caucus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961718#post961718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She has it from few days with Free Council cabal and her preAwakening studies over High Speech.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is also a problem even if she were to spend time with the free council she would have still have to paid for the merit as spending time with the free council give you the in-game justification but no the discount for the buy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961718#post961718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Where</i> did you found that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Because 'free Rotes' where always in 1E incentive to join Orders in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage The wankening pg 80 Side bar Nameless;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Some mages are Nameless; lacking membership in an Order, or having membership in a minor Order-like organization (a Nameless Order) that lacks the global scope and symbolic heft of a true Order. Nameless characters do not receive the benefits of Order membership (including Rote Skills), although larger Nameless Orders grant some of the same training; to represent these in the game, use the Mystery Cult Initiation Merit (p. 106). If that Merit is used to build a Nameless Order, it may grant a set of three Rote specialties as its third-dot benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>See this indicates what you dont gain when you made up a nameless mage. You miss all the benefits of Order membership.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage The wankening pg 80;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Order<br /> Choose your character\u2019s Order. Most characters will be in a Pentacle Order, but your Storyteller might allow Nameless or Seer of the Throne characters. Look to the chart on p. 82 to determine her three Rote Skills. Assuming your character has an Order, she receives a free dot in the Order Status Merit, a dot of Occult, and the High Speech Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here is said benefits, the 3 rote skill specializations, the dot in order status merit, the dot in occult and the high speech merit. I doesnt mention the rotes themselves. Even the Rotes section in chargen doesnt mention you dont gain them with nameless thus you should get them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961718#post961718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not see it in this example. PC is hates dearly one of Conciliors ( Khumeia from Boston ), so she cannot work with Consilium. Also, Orders just not freely teach Rotes to anyone around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it seems the player just isnt interested in your game mate. I mean you can hate a concilior and still work for the consilium at large, hell conciliours hate each other and considering how little you have to interact with a concilior as their provost do most of the day to day them just seems a feeble justification for not playing the game and you dont want to accomodate that neither. Problem is that is one of those &quot;i said, she said&quot; situation because i dont know how is your delivery of the concilium, maybe the player is in the wrong and just being difficult and contrarian or you are presenting the concilium as too overbearing, omnipotent and pushy.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T10:17:21-07:00","id":961751,"title":"","content":"Yeah I was actually just about to poke another hole in the idea of her being some kind of middleman. Consiliums exist because Nameless aren't trusted. Then there was the whole Nameless War, so you know...definitely a stigma.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> it depends, I mean if the ghost were able to initiate her into the Egregore there wouldn't really be a way for her to easily separate from or hide her initiation into the Mysterium. That doesn't mean she has an Guang Xi though, so she might still get frozen out if she doesn't fall in line somewhat and try to make friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T10:42:58-07:00","id":961778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961743#post961743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well this is a issue of mechanics over fluff, the rules indicates what a nameless doesnt start with and it doesnt mention that the PC doesnt starts with rotes. Fluff wise it depends on the individual PC, in this case if the nameless hanged out so much with the free council as to get High speech for free then it is enough justification to start with 3 rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I mentioned before - we run few day pass, between game sessions. She spend 4 days with Free Council, enough to get geist of High Speech as Yantra ( with her previous few days studies from before Awakening ). It surely is not enoght to her Rotes. Well, I assume she can <i>buy</i> Rotes from Libertines, but it will cost her, like money or Tass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961743#post961743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the whole neutral arbitrer would be more the Lictor purview as they are traveling judges that offer neutral mediation by the lex magica. I could see the silver ladder taking umbrage with the pc meddling with that or the other orders liking having a non-SL mediator.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like was mention before - Lictors and whole Mysterium is enough answer for most Consillia on 'neutral party'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961743#post961743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here is said benefits, the 3 rote skill specializations, the dot in order status merit, the dot in occult and the high speech merit. I doesnt mention the rotes themselves. Even the Rotes section in chargen doesnt mention you dont gain them with nameless thus you should get them.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>This is simply stupid!</b> I can see that Nameless can crack, on his own, High Speech ( understanding it is somehow like instinct to mages in 2E, kicking from the Awakening ) but Rotes are clearly creations of Masters and need to be <i>learned</i>. And someone need to teach the Nameless PC them, she cannot 'guess' Rotes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T11:39:52-07:00","id":961799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961778#post961778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>This is simply stupid!</b> I can see that Nameless can crack, on his own, High Speech ( understanding it is somehow like instinct to mages in 2E, kicking from the Awakening ) but Rotes are clearly creations of Masters and need to be <i>learned</i>. And someone need to teach the Nameless PC them, she cannot 'guess' Rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, that raw so take it to the devs but secondly, i think you are missunderstanding something important about Chargen in mage, it isnt for newly awakened mages. Chargen gives you a newly stablished mage who has been around at least a few month after awakening if not more.<br /> <br /> He doesnt learn rotes on his &quot;own&quot; but there is a multitude of ways to justify starting a nameless with a a few rotes before play. From the top of my head<ul><li>He had a short time mentor.</li> <li>He hang around as a prospect member of an order before calling it quits.</li> <li>Found a low powered grimmoire (meanin it only had the low level rotes he started with) and he lost it.</li> <li>He did something that another mage owe him a favor so he taugh him those low level rotes.</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961778#post961778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I mentioned before - we run few day pass, between game sessions. She spend 4 days with Free Council, enough to get geist of High Speech as Yantra ( with her previous few days studies from before Awakening ). It surely is not enoght to her Rotes. Well, I assume she can <i>buy</i> Rotes from Libertines, but it will cost her, like money or Tass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now <b>this is simply silly!</b>. 4 days to learn high speech? If it was a background thing with not exact time frame sure but 4 days? Having a intuitive understanding of something is not the same as learning is 4 days. Besides you cannot learn high speech before awakening neither because its just giberish. I find it funny that learning a secret language in 4 days is completely plausible to you but learning rotes, which btw are basically mnemonic techniques designed to be easier to learn and memorize, completely breaks the suspension of disbelief. <br /> <br /> If you are running 2E and your game started with newly awakened pcs without orders (as you mention you rp the initiations) then nobody should have gotten rotes, free speech and/or order status for free from the get got. If you started with chargen mages (meaning newly awakened but with some months under their belts, and already into orders somewhat) then this player (the nameless) should have payed for getting high speech from the free council and not for free but should have started with rotes if you wanna force him to spend xp to get something she should get by raw because &quot;reasons&quot; thats pulling the rug under her feet which is not gonna help with her predisposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-01-2016, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:14:15-07:00","id":961821,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants\">You understand now that High Speech is like filter to seeing Symbols</a> and if character is having enough materials - like Grimoire and few days with mages liking to usage - she should get it automatically, right? High Speech in 2E is like Mage Sight - you get it from Day 0 after Awakening. Also, 'singing' Yantra is so instinctual to many cultures, PC in question used this kind things even preAwakening with 'Sleeper' rituals of ephemera binding. Really, adding High Speech to 'singing' is not really that difficult, especially as you have living examples of merry Free Councils wanting to add shanties to their spellcasting.<br /> <br /> High Speech is not now 'secret language of Atlantis' it was in 1E - it's more 'instinctual filter to understand Symbol-Runes in reality' in 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:37:11-07:00","id":961840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961821#post961821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants&quot;]You</a> understand now that High Speech is like filter to seeing Symbols[/URL] and if character is having enough materials - like Grimoire and few days with mages liking to usage - she should get it automatically, right? High Speech in 2E is like Mage Sight - you get it from Day 0 after Awakening. Also, 'singing' Yantra is so instinctual to many cultures, PC in question used this kind things even preAwakening with 'Sleeper' rituals of ephemera binding. Really, adding High Speech to 'singing' is not really that difficult, especially as you have living examples of merry Free Councils wanting to add shanties to their spellcasting.<br /> <br /> High Speech is not now 'secret language of Atlantis' it was in 1E - it's more 'instinctual filter to understand Symbol-Runes in reality' in 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet the merit cost 1 point and nameless dont start with it. You can justify how &quot;easy&quot; is to learn to use it as a yantra all you want but you dont start with the merit from awakening day 0 as is plain obvious in both the nameless description and the merit cost. And if you gonna houserule it as the nameless get it for free but then you gonna houserule it as to rip him off from the free rotes she should get that is<br /> <br /> A) the realm of houserules.<br /> <br /> B) a conversation you should have with the player not with us.<br /> <br /> Saying learning high speech as a yantra is easy but low level rotes arent is silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":".  Syntaxis error that change the meaning 09-01-2016, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:43:10-07:00","id":961843,"title":"","content":"Mages understand High Speech since the moment of their Awakening. High Speech merit isn't about that. It's about perfecting it into a yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:50:48-07:00","id":961849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961843#post961843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages understand High Speech since the moment of their Awakening. High Speech merit isn't about that. It's about perfecting it into a yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im talking about the merit in this case. Even the book says it take time to teach how to apply high speech to yantras, so assuming the absurdily low time of 4 days to learn the merit is jarring that the same frame of time cant be use to learn the starting rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:52:22-07:00","id":961851,"title":"","content":"I understand that. It seems that Wyrd thinks that understanding High Speech = High Speech merit. High Speech merit is like understanding how to poetry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T13:32:21-07:00","id":961869,"title":"","content":"Merit means High Speech as Yantra discovery. If character:<br /> 1) Long background history in vocalized rituals preAwakening,<br /> 2) Has living examples with living mages for few days that like to use it.<br /> <br /> I do not see a problem for her to get it.<br /> <br /> More even, I do not see a problem for normal PC to get Merit in time of week of extensive training from Order - but I see whole Orders introduction ( chargen characters ) as more matter of month at large, so my 'learning times' can not work with many STs POV.<br /> <br /> Still, clue is this - if High Speech Yantra is like poetry, <i>anyone</i> (Awakened) can try it, just like anyone can ryhm. Orders can easily teach you this. Nameless can hammer it if she knows what she is looking for. But Rotes are encoded by Masters, with their Reaches - and so Rotes can <i>only</i> be teached by someone or from something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-01-2016, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T13:48:30-07:00","id":961880,"title":"","content":"Then get creative about &quot;how someone without access to masters and teachers got to know their rotes&quot;? It's a fantastic plot hook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T23:17:30-07:00","id":962121,"title":"","content":"So, if this is an out of game problem there's no solution possible inside the game. If the player doesn't want to participate, you can't make them. If the player isn't interested in what the game's about, then they won't really be able to play it. If they've accidentally made a character that can't fit with the group, it may be time to offer for them to retire that character and make a new one.<br /> <br /> However you can make interesting stories about the nameless, so if that works for you, the player and the rest of the group then here's some ideas for story-hooks.<br /> <br /> What happens when the nameless is researching the occult in the library and starts seeing other people borrowing the same books? <br /> What happens if those other people are a hunter group who mistakenly believes the mage is a hunter like them and tries recruiting them? <br /> What happens when the nameless mage finds an artifact during the story (not something they've spent XP on, due to sanctity of merits) and then a much more powerful Mysterium mage challenges them to a duel arcane for possession of the artifact? Who will speak up for the nameless mage in political circles?<br /> What happens if the nameless mage, perhaps due to that previous encounter with the hunters, gets accused of being a banisher?<br /> What happens when a high ranking provost believes that there's corruption and a conspiracy within the pentacle orders and doesn't know who to trust... so they confide in the nameless mage since they've rejected all the orders?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T23:21:27-07:00","id":962123,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6748_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6748\" data-vbnamecard=\"6748\">Michael Kenner</a> , those story hooks are really cool and could help to solve our problem in long way!<br /> <br /> I think that if PC goes for the 'ghost mage mentoring' she will get all Order benefits - beside Order Status in it and by this, Order Merit. If she will want more, she will need to get to living Caucus of Order to get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T23:42:50-07:00","id":962131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=962123#post962123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6748_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6748\" data-vbnamecard=\"6748\">Michael Kenner</a> , those story hooks are really cool and could help to solve our problem in long way!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome, I hope they help. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T01:59:00-07:00","id":962161,"title":"","content":"Nameless can use rotes in Grimoires (with the lengthened casting time) normally. They can't buy rotes they can cast in a hurry with xp unless someone has taught them the mnemonic compression techniques the Orders use - we'll get into this in Signs of Sorcery, but for your purposes you can assume that those come with Order Rote Skills.<br /> <br /> If the character was (briefly) a Free Council trainee, she could have their rote skills and be able to compress rotes.<br /> <br /> We don't have a Merit for &quot;can use rotes&quot;; Nameless Orders like the Tremere who use Mystery Cult Initiation get their rote skills *instead* of the third dot benefit. It's entirely up to you if she does or doesn't know how to do it, but fluff-wise it's one of the first things a mentor will teach you (yea, before High Speech!) as the Orders like to tempt would-be initiates with rotes.<br /> <br /> As for High Speech, mages inherently understand it as part of their template, but using it to describe your imago as a yantra is a specific skill; it's like the difference between being able to draw and being able to lay out blueprints. All six Orders do make sure their members are trained in it, but many Nameless learn how to do it by watching other mages cast or experimenting with Speech on their own. Which is represented by buying the Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T05:54:28-07:00","id":962212,"title":"","content":"To clarify - Nameless are assumed to have or not have starting Rotes after chargen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T06:50:32-07:00","id":962235,"title":"","content":"He just said, they are not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T06:56:18-07:00","id":962239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=962212#post962212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify - Nameless are assumed to have or not have starting Rotes after chargen?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Only if they have 3 dots of mystery cult initiation with the nameless order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T08:04:17-07:00","id":962290,"title":"","content":"Isn't this Consilium one where the Hierarch wants everyone to be fighting each other and is basically an Exarch-stand in for divide and conquer? Someone like that could take interest in injecting extra distrust into the Consilium by inviting Nameless into it, while knowing that individual Nameless lack backing of the Order and thus became much easier to control and punish (no one will yell at you for kicking them in the gut). <br /> Imagine how paranoid people would become if drunk Nemean would decide &quot;OK, this random nameless Mage will become my tool, let's everyone think she is my favorite, grahahahahaha.&quot; <br /> Sentinel who is loyal only to him and has no Order to support or political party to push sound like a good minion to groom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T08:40:17-07:00","id":962308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=962290#post962290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't this Consilium one where the Hierarch wants everyone to be fighting each other and is basically an Exarch-stand in for divide and conquer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not anymore, Wyrd's been running the game in a post-Nemean version of Boston.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T19:52:05-07:00","id":962649,"title":"","content":"I've only skimmed the order books so I can't argue them, but from everything else I always got the impression that new mages joined an order not so much because they were browbeaten into doing so, but because they were drawn to the order that shared their desires and goals. You don't join the Mysterium because the rules say you have to, you don't even join because membership will give you greater access to their libraries (though that would add to its appeal), no you join because you want to interact and debate with other people who share your hunger for learning and belief in the importance of saving knowledge. That's why the Mysterium has the most academics, the Arrow the most police officers and former soldiers, while the Guardians have a lot of members who bear scars from the misuse of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T20:15:32-07:00","id":962659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=962649#post962649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've only skimmed the order books so I can't argue them, but from everything else I always got the impression that new mages joined an order not so much because they were browbeaten into doing so, but because they were drawn to the order that shared their desires and goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the stuff about Mages getting pushed towards joining orders is in Sanctum and Sigil, which has a lot of cool ideas for Mage politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T21:03:01-07:00","id":962675,"title":"","content":"The Orders are really good at identifying who they might be able to get to identify with them if even on only a tangential level. As you interact with its members though it's likely to start shaping your worldview and you slowly sink deeper into their ideologies and find your niche inside them. It's the same as being in any social group, as you interact with people who are mostly like minded your beliefs that you had before become self-reinforcing and you're more willing to accept additional beliefs presented to you by the group because the original trust invested allows it to pass a sort of unspoken veracity test. Just being in an Order long enough helps you to start seeing things from their point of view, and the trust you place in them allows you to weight their opinions due to personal bias. Orders don't need to browbeat you into taking their beliefs as gospel anymore than any organization does. The best kind of buy-in is the one where you don't feel like you have to be convinced at all until you can't remember or can't recognize where your beliefs begin and the Order's ends.<br /> <br /> This is pretty clearly realized by the way the Orders tier their beliefs because they're mystery religions. At first they get you in on the ground floor with some things you agree with and then as you deepen your interactions and understanding of the Orders you start to find out more about their ultimate beliefs and tenets.<br /> <br /> A Guardian of the Veil that's just starting out might be informed about the Heiromagus, but he's not necessarily informed about the system by which the GotV believe the Heiromagus will be brought about (The Diamond Wheel) and how that justifies their right to kill. The Mysterium will entice you with a greater understanding of mystic lore but only as you move deeper will you learn about their beliefs in the causes of Pancryptia, and their inherent bias against Sleepers as a result pf their attempts to fight it. The Silver Ladder proselytizes the need to raise up all of humanity to fight the Lie, but only as you go deeper do you find out that it means they're equipping -you- to rule and that they firmly believe you have the right. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-03-2016, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}